 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T08:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**For a healthy adult, a short, easy ride looks reasonable based on the latest reading—but I’d skip a hard or long ride.** Kuching’s Department of Environment-linked API was **65 (moderate) at 8:00 a.m. today, October 17**, and has ranged 64–72 over the past 24 hours. That’s a morning reading, not a guarantee for this evening, so check APIMS again before setting out. ([semakapi.my](https://semakapi.my/en/kuching))\n\nIf you have asthma or heart/lung disease—or are older, pregnant, or taking a child—be more cautious and avoid strenuous cycling. Malaysia’s Health Ministry advises reducing strenuous outdoor activity once API exceeds 100. ([moh.gov.my](https://www.moh.gov.my/teras/info-kesihatan/jerebu/artikel-dan-panduan-pengguna-berkaitan-jerebu/langkah-langkah-pencegahan-semasa-jerebu?utm_source=openai))\n\nOne other concern: **thunderstorms are forecast around 8–9 p.m.** Don’t ride during a storm, and head home if the haze worsens or you develop coughing, wheezing, or irritation. ",
